    },
    {
     "title": "Covariance vs correlation",
     "takeaway": "Covariance tells you only the direction two variables move together, while correlation scales it to the range −1 to +1 so you also get the strength.",
     "path": "notes/data-science/statistics/descriptive/covariance-vs-correlation.md",
     "day": "2026-11-07",
