    {
     "title": "Skewness and kurtosis",
     "takeaway": "Skewness measures how lopsided a distribution is, which shows up as the gap between mean and median, and kurtosis measures how heavy its tails are compared with its centre.",
     "path": "notes/data-science/statistics/descriptive/skewness-and-kurtosis.md",
     "day": "2026-11-07",
     "kind": "note",
