    {
     "title": "Types of data and types of statistics",
     "takeaway": "Descriptive statistics summarise the data you have and inferential statistics generalise from a sample to a population, while data itself is either categorical (nominal or ordinal) or numerical (discrete or continuous).",
     "path": "notes/data-science/statistics/descriptive/types-of-data-and-statistics.md",
