     "title": "Confidence intervals, z-test and t-test",
     "takeaway": "A confidence interval is the point estimate ± a margin of error. Use z when the population SD is known and t (with df = n − 1) when it isn't.",
     "path": "notes/data-science/statistics/inferential/confidence-intervals-z-and-t.md",
