     "title": "P-value, significance and Type I/II errors",
     "takeaway": "If p ≤ 0.05, reject H₀. A Type I error rejects a true H₀ (a false positive), and a Type II error keeps a false H₀ (a false negative).",
     "path": "notes/data-science/statistics/inferential/p-value-and-errors.md",
