     "title": "Common distributions: uniform, normal, Bernoulli",
     "takeaway": "In a normal distribution 68%, 95% and 99.7% of the data falls within 1, 2 and 3 SDs of the mean. Uniform gives every outcome equal odds, and Bernoulli has only the outcomes 0 and 1.",
